  "body": "## What happened\n\nPosting can hold a program when the machined stock already has a low area in the incoming stock. This can occur when the current setup uses a casting or unfinished stock from an earlier operation. The hold can occur even when this program leaves the low area at its incoming height.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Use a stock mesh with a step below the surface of the nominal part.\n2. Add a cut away from the step. Mark the mesh as raw stock only.\n3. Post the setup. The deviation check reports the step as a gouge.\n4. For a negative control, add a cut that deepens the step.\n\n## Version and environment\n\nTarget base is CamCraft v0.26.0. The reproduction uses a synthetic stepped mesh and the headless posting tests on Windows.\n\n## Done means\n\nPosting holds by default. An explicit setup-session acknowledgment can permit posting if a matching stock simulation shows the same deficient cells at their incoming heights. The report gives the count, maximum depth and location. New or deeper deficits still hold posting. Reopening the project clears the acknowledgment.\n\nSuggested triage is P3 and effort:high because this changes a posting safety check.\r\n",
